# Build outputs
target/
target-ide/

# Quinoa's own node installation, from the `-Dquarkus.quinoa.package-manager-install=true` that only
# docker/Dockerfile's builder stage passes — so a local build never creates this, and that is exactly
# why it is easy to commit by accident from a machine that once did. It stays listed because the
# entry costs nothing and `.dockerignore` keeping it out of the build CONTEXT is the part that
# matters. Unanchored because install-dir is resolved against the *project root Quinoa finds*, which
# is the first ancestor of the module's target/ holding a src/main — `service/`, not the repo root.
.quinoa/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
.project
.classpath
.factorypath
.settings/
*.iml

# OS
.DS_Store

# Home-relative caches a tool leaks into the repo root when run with the repo as its cwd
.cache/
.m2/
.local/

# Local per-machine Quarkus config overrides — the address of a locally-run qits-projects, and a
# port that does not collide with its siblings. Quarkus reads .env from the process's working
# directory at ordinal 295, above the packaged application.properties (250). Never committed; the
# tracked .env.example beside it is the template. Same convention as qits-projects.
.env

# Claude Code session state (worktrees, local settings). Never committed.
.claude/
